- Local-only portfolio demo. No hosting, Render, Docker, cloud, public endpoint, authentication, database, frontend, payment integration or real data.
- Python 3.11+. Use uv with a venv in .venv and requirements.txt via `uv pip install -r requirements.txt`. Do not create pyproject.toml, use `uv add`, or create uv.lock.
- MCP server and client use the standalone `fastmcp` package at the version pinned in requirements.txt. Read the installed package's docs/source before coding. Never import from the official `mcp` package's `mcp.server.fastmcp` or mix APIs from other versions.
- Transport is stdio. The server must never print to stdout; log to stderr only.
- Exactly 8 MCP tools. Do not add more.
- Secrets: never open, read, print or log .env. Never ask me to paste keys. Load GROQ_API_KEY via python-dotenv/os.environ. .env.example holds placeholders only.
- Never run git commit, git push or any remote git command. I do that manually.
- All data is fabricated. Label every invented business rule as a demo assumption.
- Keep code beginner-readable. Ask before adding dependencies.
- Never claim something runs or passes unless you actually ran it.